What is vendored
----------------

  include/cuobjclient.h
      cuObjClient public API header, v1.2.0. The only NVIDIA header
      elbencho includes directly (source/toolkits/CuObjClientTk.h).

  include/cufile.h
      cuFile (GPUDirect Storage) public API header, required by
      cuobjclient.h.

  include/cuda.h
      CUDA driver API header, required for the type declarations
      (CUdeviceptr, CUstream, ...) that appear in the cuFile and
      cuObject API signatures.

  lib/{x86_64,aarch64}/libcuobjclient.so.1.2.0  (and SONAME aliases)
      NVIDIA cuObjClient shared library, v1.2.0.

  lib/{x86_64,aarch64}/libcufile.so.1.18.0      (and SONAME aliases)
  lib/{x86_64,aarch64}/libcufile_rdma.so.1.18.0 (and SONAME aliases)
      NVIDIA cuFile shared libraries, v1.18.0.

The header set was taken from the same NVIDIA 1.2.0 drop as the
libraries. cuobjclient.h carries two modifications, both removals of
material that is not NVIDIA's: an s3_rdma_client_ctx struct and the two
`#include` lines it needed. The include of the cuFile header was renamed
to match the file name used here. Nothing else was changed.


Version pairing
---------------

libcuobjclient must be wire-compatible with the cuObject version of the
S3 server it talks to. 1.2.0 here pairs with libcuobjserver 1.2.0 on the
server side. Do not mix versions — a mismatch shows up as RDMA buffer
registration failures or transfer retry exhaustion even though the HTTP
control request succeeds.


